      },
      "lineNbr": 239,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-10T20:39:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Maybe we need a lock on writing out to make sure we don\u0027t have concurrent writes that could corrupt the disk file\n\nThis part should already be fine. BlobCache store/load pointers go to DawnCachingBackend and that is [thread safe](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/dawn_caching_interface.cc;l\u003d180-209;drc\u003d7b12b4fd45f1a2570d0f29041c74f8497095bf28). The store to disk goes through [this](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:gpu/command_buffer/service/dawn_caching_interface.cc;l\u003d44-49;drc\u003d7b12b4fd45f1a2570d0f29041c74f8497095bf28) which sends an IPC so that guarantees the stores to disk happen sequentially.",
      "parentUuid": "f77656be_7c836326",
      "revId": "a72295c64f6014a4a66c0a7731912c04af8de0e0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
